    {
      "id": 171742,
      "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
      "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-04-10T04:21:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That looks great. &nbsp;Will the normal (non-canonical) tiles have a similar artistic look to them, or did the final product stick with the patterns we saw during playtesting?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It's been said in a couple of places that the regular tiles will have a simpler and less artistic design than the canonical map, because while the more decorative map is beautiful, it is also it harder to read, and makes the board more cluttered. &nbsp;While the regular tiles might not be exactly the same patterns that we saw, they will be much closer to those than they will be to the canonical map.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:54:30.488Z",
